From: Yocto User <yoctouser@workspace.local>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/arm-smmu-v3: shrink queues for embedded microvisor

Dramatically shrink the memory allocated for ARM SMMUv3 hardware queues,
freeing ~8 MB of RAM on boot. This is highly specific to our static VFIO context.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [embedded hypervisor optimization]

---
 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu-v3/arm-smmu-v3.h | 6 +-----
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu-v3/arm-smmu-v3.h b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu-v3/arm-smmu-v3.h
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu-v3/arm-smmu-v3.h
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu-v3/arm-smmu-v3.h
@@ -207,9 +207,5 @@
 
 /* Ensure DMA allocations are naturally aligned */
-#ifdef CONFIG_CMA_ALIGNMENT
-#define Q_MAX_SZ_SHIFT			(PAGE_SHIFT + CONFIG_CMA_ALIGNMENT)
-#else
-#define Q_MAX_SZ_SHIFT			(PAGE_SHIFT + MAX_PAGE_ORDER)
-#endif
+#define Q_MAX_SZ_SHIFT			11
 
 /*
